# Project standards

## Communication

- Answer the user in French.
- Write all code comments in English.
- Do not use emoticons in comments or code.

## Code changes

- Change only what the task requires. No drive-by refactors or unrelated edits.
- Prefer small, focused diffs. Reuse existing patterns, names, and file layout.
- Avoid acronyms in identifiers (variable, function, type names) when a clear full phrase fits.

## Explaining code in chat

When referencing existing code in messages, use Cursor code citations with line numbers and path:
`startLine:endLine:filepath`
